# A capacitor charging through a resistor.
#
# Click the switch to close it. The capacitor's voltage rises quickly at first and then more and more
# slowly, as the voltage left across the resistor, and so the current, shrinks: after one time
# constant, R × C = 10 kΩ × 100 µF = 1 s, it has reached 63% of the battery's 9 V. Open the switch
# and the capacitor keeps its charge; there is nowhere for it to go.

speed 1

battery   B1  0 0  0 6  9V
switch    S1  0 0  3 0
resistor  R1  3 0  7 0  10k
capacitor C1  7 0  7 6  100u
wire          7 6  0 6
ground        0 6
meter     M1  7 0  7 6
meter     M2  3 0  7 0
